% A comparison of constants is tested before the rule reads anything, once
% for the rule rather than once for each tuple it goes on to read.  Its note
% is the rule's, as one a comparison of bound values makes is: early names
% the first comparison it makes, which rejects every binding, late names
% the one it makes after its own test of constants holds, and kept, whose
% tests hold, derives what it reads.  Answers are unchanged.
v(1).
v(2).
w(a).
early(X) :- w(a), 1 < a, v(X).
late(X) :- 3 > 2, v(X), X > b.
kept(X) :- w(a), 2 > 1, v(X).

early(X)?
late(X)?
kept(X)?
